1785606587433826	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEymgc		item.comment	bn-2he	{"body":"Delivered in .maw/workspaces/bn-2he @ 0b49b9d. (1) AUTHORITATIVE LINE COUNTER: tools/check_kernel_covenant.py, method documented in its module docstring — counted files = crates/continuum-kernel-*/src/**/*.rs (tests/benches/examples excluded); a file declared '#[cfg(test)] mod NAME;' excluded whole (the four fixture.rs, 1,504 lines); every #[cfg(test)] item excluded in place, brace-matched OR ';'-terminated by a comment/string/rawstring/char/lifetime-aware scanner (the ';' case is exactly the 8-line disagreement: waiting for a brace after 'mod fixture;' swallows the following pub-use block); a line = every surviving physical line, blanks and comments included. Number: 8,495 as landed (core 1,868 / sat 2,092 / smt 2,131 / temporal 2,404) and 10,667 with this bone's receipt modules (2,406/2,625/2,687/2,949), budget 15,000, headroom 4,333. (2) RECEIPTS: a receipt module per crate emitting proof-receipt.schema.json instances; golden receipt per crate asserted byte-for-byte in the crate's unit tests and validated against the schema by KCOV-09. Epoch naming resolves concern (b): WIRE_EPOCH_ID = '<crate>/<magic>/<epoch>' (continuum-kernel-core/CONTCERT/1 etc.), carried in checker.version, NEVER in 'epochs' — RFC 0026 correction 17 says there is no checker epoch and a native checker's identity is engine identity. Build digest/toolchain/input digest/observers/proof epoch/receipt id/reproduce are an explicit Seam the caller supplies; the kernel shape-checks them and names them as trusted inputs; no digest is computed or faked. (3) MUTATION MATRIX: tools/kernel-covenant/mutation-matrix.toml, 23 classes x 4 crates = 92 cells, indexing the existing sweeps (not duplicating them); KCOV-08 fail-closed on a named test that does not exist or a cell with no test and no waiver. 86 owned, 4 permanently not-applicable, 2 uncovered gaps: envelope.digest-relabelling in kernel-smt and kernel-temporal (core and sat both have the test; porting it is follow-up crate work outside this bone's fence). --strict promotes uncovered cells to failures. (4) 9 requirements KCOV-01..09, 21 violating fixtures, all caught by --self-test; wired as 'just covenant' into 'just check'. Full 'just check' exits 0."}	blake3:gB7RjYtWycLIEtSnZkWE24oL8mPi9OEOZorw257hRsE
1785606689520936	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEymwc		item.comment	bn-2he	{"body":"Landed @ 5ca30d3. Lead ran the covenant self-test + real run and all four kernel suites in-workspace. Ratified: the counting method (physical lines, cfg(test) excluded incl. the ;-terminated-mod case that explains the 8-line discrepancy — one authority now, 10,667/15,000); receipts carrying wire-epoch identity as semver build metadata NOT an epoch (RFC 0026 correction 17 respected; the START_HERE 'checker epoch' phrase resolved as alias); smt's assurance_class derived from lemma use and absent from the seam so TRUSTED_SOLVER cannot be hidden; receipts only for Verified; checker.independent rightly omitted (pair property). Fail-closed matrix with waiver-cannot-outlive-gap. Two uncovered cells + two schema gaps routed to follow-up bones. PR-9 exit call is mine: all six IMPL leaves satisfied — exit evidence bone next."}	blake3:M95fMHTahoNFxp0HxAOhWGfv4e7xDKt7ryi3b3qq7TI
