1785606691870601	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEynQc		item.create	bn-1q4r7	{"description":"# Context\nbn-2he's mutation matrix has two uncovered cells: envelope.digest-relabelling in continuum-kernel-smt and continuum-kernel-temporal. core and sat both have envelope_digests_are_carried_labels_not_facts_the_kernel_can_check; port it to the other two. tools/check_kernel_covenant.py --strict promotes the gap to a failure — after the port, --strict should pass and the two 'uncovered' waiver rows come OUT of mutation-matrix.toml.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Both tests exist and pass; matrix rows flip to owned; --strict passes.\n- [ ] just check green.","kind":"task","title":"Port envelope-relabelling mutation test to kernel-smt and kernel-temporal"}	blake3:FOkq-6oduLxgHQqvdQ9-2YbjwVjYkZDrTDABYQeCWm4
1785606692064524	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyngc		item.create	bn-ww5ic	{"description":"# Context\nTwo gaps bn-2he surfaced in schemas/proof-receipt.schema.json: (1) certificate.kind closes at ten members with no state-typing member, so kernel-core's two families both report closed-set with the distinction in prose; (2) no field for assurance class or trusted components, forcing them into claim.text — RFC 0005 forbids bare 'verified', so these deserve typed fields. Draft-epoch narrowing/addition is allowed pre-freeze.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] certificate.kind gains the state-type member (or the sharing is ratified in the schema $comment with reason).\n- [ ] Typed assurance_class and trusted_components fields added; the four golden receipts + receipt modules updated together (coordinate: this touches kernel crates too — one bone, one workspace).\n- [ ] Dossier validator + covenant KCOV-09 green.","kind":"task","title":"proof-receipt schema: state-type kind and assurance/trusted-components fields"}	blake3:n4F7oX1ENd6dnyfKAlK8dtR21NJ6sGVIlSHxcHADXvQ
