1785624405833916	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyqgg		item.comment	bn-1gc	{"body":"Landed @ b68d8dd (workspace bn-1gc). Budget accounting + committed-partial-evidence accounting in crates/continuum-task/src/budget/ (budget.rs, budget/dimension.rs, budget/partial.rs) + 3 integration test files. region.rs untouched.\n\nLEDGER / SD-12. CostDimension spells the nine (wall_ms, cpu_ms, memory_bytes, states, solver_ms, proof_ms, tokens, candidates, bytes) in IDL declaration order. Not forked: tests/budget_dimensions.rs holds it to three independently maintained sources — the IDL's struct Budget (order), RFC 0026's prose enumeration in 'Cost and omissions' (order), and verification-task.schema.json's budget properties + additionalProperties:false (set) — with the_check_is_not_vacuous mutating each source (rename / drop / F16's tenth 'transitions' dimension) and requiring each comparison to break. Wire encoding stays in continuumd/src/protocol/envelope.rs; agreement is by shared token, the WorkerState::status_token device, since plan §20 gives this crate no continuumd edge.\n\nOMISSION DISCIPLINE (INV-007). MeterSet separates declared from enforced; the 2x2 is total. declared+metered = enforced. declared+unmetered = typed DimensionOmission carrying subject 'budget.<token>' and reason token 'unsupported' — bn-18z's exact spelling in verification::unenforced — AND a charge is refused outright, because recording spend for something nothing measured invents a measurement RFC 0026 requires to be absent. undeclared+metered = measured, never exhausts. undeclared+unmetered = inert, owes nothing. MeterSet::STATES_ONLY reproduces continuumd's eight hand-written omissions by derivation rather than by array.\n\nSEMANTICS. Spend is monotone and irrevocable; only headroom is refundable. charge records what happened; reserve/settle/release hold and hand back budget for a publication in flight, so a discarded artifact refunds its bytes without refunding the compute. A settle can never exhaust (the reservation already held the headroom) — hence it returns the refund, not a ChargeOutcome, because an unreachable arm is worse than no arm. Exhaustion is a RESULT (ChargeOutcome::Exhausted), never an error — bfs::Exploration::Exhausted's shape — naming dimension/limit/spent/requested plus the ErrorCode token BudgetExhausted, and never a verdict. BudgetFault is structural only. Ledger remembers the FIRST exhausted dimension (Partial::tripped's discipline).\n\nMID-FLIGHT UPDATE. The RFC ADMITS lowering — it defines it, and the definition is suspension, not refusal. Five arms as a value: Raised / Unchanged / Tightened / Suspend(B18) / Unenforced, walked as a 9-row data table. 'Committed spend' read as recorded non-refundable spend rather than spend-at-last-checkpoint; the alternative admits a ceiling the run has already passed, which is retroactive truncation (test: lowering_between_the_checkpoint_and_the_live_spend_still_parks). The ceiling is recorded on EVERY arm because TaskRecord.budget reports the budget in force.\n\nPARTIAL EVIDENCE + OBLIGATION INTEGRATION. Checkpoint = (region layer's monotone committed count, Spend at that moment) — the only place the two vocabularies meet. CommittedPartialEvidence reports committed / spend_at_commit / total_spend / uncommitted_spend; the last is real spend against no artifact and neither layer can compute it alone. No second obligation ledger was opened — the region layer's stays the single answer. Instead EvidenceBook::reconcile is a THIRD independently computed accounting beside Finalization::is_total's two: commitments == checkpoints, no dangling reservation (the budget-side reading of 'committed or absent', off headroom rather than off the tree), no unaccounted/unknown worker.\n\nTESTS. 54 new (29 unit + 9 dimensions + 8 update + 7 partial-evidence). The partial-evidence sweep runs 210 interleavings x 8 cancellation-completes positions = 1,680 runs, each asserting totality, reconciliation, committed-count agreement between the layers, and the omission travelling with the evidence; anti-vacuity guards on run count, on at-least-one-committed, and on >1 distinct canonical rendering. Determinism as byte-identity on Reconciliation::render and BudgetLedger::render.\n\nANNOTATIONS. PR-6-IMPL-03 (budget accounting) CLAIMED, with two non-claims stated in the annotation: this crate ships no meters (nothing reads a clock or counts a byte), and continuumd is not rewired (outside the fence) — the seam is designed and written down in budget.rs. PR-6-IMPL-02 (committed partial evidence) DECLINED and named in START_HERE with what it waits on: the bone's own criterion is durability across daemon restart, and both ledgers COUNT publications rather than naming them (no continuum-workspace edge; plan §20 states none), so there is no artifact identity to persist. What landed is the accounting of committed partial evidence, not the artifact.\n\nGATE. just check exit 0. All 77 pre-existing continuum-task tests pass unchanged (28 unit + 15 + 10 + 15 + 8 integration + 1 doctest at HEAD); region.rs has zero diff.\n\nCONCERNS FOR THE LEAD. (1) CostDimension's home: it sits in continuum-task because the fence scoped me there, but continuum-value is the workspace's declared vocabulary leaf and already holds AssuranceDimension::ALL, which RFC 0026 cites by name. If a second crate needs the nine, promoting CostDimension to continuum-value is the move, and it is a pure relocation. (2) The 'committed spend' reading in task.update_budget is a genuine interpretive choice; it is stated in the module and pinned by a test, and it governs whether a lowering parks or tightens. (3) Suspension is a budget-layer fact and the region layer cannot represent a task that parks under it and survives teardown — the same constraint bn-2gk's concern 2 recorded for the rewiring bone."}	blake3:iZFmMpqo0qOcUJFPCT4xojU1Zp9HXmXFC1RzA037_Us
1785624912434180	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyqwg		item.comment	bn-12t	{"body":"Landed @ 1807d7f. Lead ran all 15 continuumd suites in-workspace (221 tests green). Ratified: the parked-continuation resolution with its four RFC citations (a parked continuation is not a live worker; resume mints fresh in a strictly-later region — the rejected alternative is DX-14's own leak); scoped-as-only-entry making no-region-outlives-its-dispatch structural; defects-recorded-not-raised turning the region layer into a checker of the daemon's operation order; the wire-visibility audit (provable equality + debug_assert pin). The resume-after-cancel finding accepted as landed behavior (ok/status=cancelled with proven no-work — not a new code; wire-visible changes need the flag discipline). The region-tree unbounded-growth question recorded alongside admissions as the daemon-durability deferred pair. GOV-1-07-forced rationale entry accepted (the gate demanded it)."}	blake3:WjEF3WiKH_fh_9lUE9C5NmPQWlVKEmSz2TUmkk6QuYo
