1785694431470570	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyrQg		item.comment	bn-1gc	{"body":"Rebase reconciliation (workspace synced onto bn-12t mid-flight; commits are now e0688dc feat, 81a8e50 maw structured resolve, 8612a49 chore).\n\nbn-12t landed the daemon rewiring and claimed PR-6-IMPL-01 (task lifecycle) and IMPL-04 (suspension/continuation) while I was in flight, so START_HERE's PR-6 block conflicted. Resolved with 'maw ws resolve bn-1gc --keep epoch', which preserved both sides' cleanly-merged hunks: bn-12t's IMPL-01/IMPL-04 annotations and my IMPL-03 annotation and 'committed partial evidence is not annotated' paragraph all survive. One hand edit after the resolve: the intro sentence read 'Two things these annotations deliberately do not claim' but now heads three paragraphs, the third of which (bn-12t's rewrite of the task-lifecycle paragraph) explains a bullet that MOVED from unclaimed to claimed rather than a non-claim. Reworded to 'Two things these annotations deliberately do not claim, and one bullet that changed hands between bones; the honest reading needs all three.' Traceability regenerated after the resolve; PLAN_REQUIREMENTS.json needed no change (the structured merge already carried both sides).\n\nPR-6 is now IMPL-01/03/04/05/06 satisfied, IMPL-02 the only open bullet.\n\nRe-verified on the rebased tree: full 'just check' exit 0 (155 green test-result lines), continuum-task 131 tests, continuumd 15 suites green. Note bn-12t's continuumd rewiring now depends on continuum-task; my additions are purely additive to that crate and region.rs has zero diff, so nothing of bn-12t's was disturbed.\n\nOne thing bn-12t's arrival changes for the lead to weigh: continuumd now has a live task-lifecycle join, so the budget seam I documented in budget.rs (TaskEntry holds a BudgetLedger; bounds_of becomes a projection of its states ceiling; verification::unenforced is deleted in favour of BudgetLedger::omissions; task.update_budget reads UpdateOutcome) is now a concrete follow-on against real code rather than a hypothetical one. That follow-on is also what would let IMPL-02 be claimed, since it is where an artifact identity could be persisted."}	blake3:giPhTp0DNaElBKvxJ_ZSgfMqLy1rjB3JtBkmpeJAsUM
1785694664835587	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyrgg		item.create	bn-23j7s	{"description":"# Context\nbn-1gc landed the budget calculus in crates/continuum-task/src/budget/ (nine-dimension ledger, MeterSet omission discipline, five-arm task.update_budget legality table, Checkpoint/CommittedPartialEvidence/EvidenceBook::reconcile) and documented the daemon seam in budget.rs. bn-12t landed the region rewiring, so the join is against real code. This bone is that join, and it is what makes PR-6 IMPL-02 claimable: bn-1gc's ledgers COUNT publications rather than naming them (continuum-task declares no continuum-workspace edge; plan §20 states none), so artifact identity and restart durability are continuumd's to add.\n\n# Scope (the seam as written in budget.rs)\n- TaskEntry holds a BudgetLedger; bounds_of becomes a projection of its states ceiling.\n- verification::unenforced is DELETED in favour of BudgetLedger::omissions (MeterSet::STATES_ONLY reproduces the eight hand-written omissions by derivation — keep the derivation, not the array).\n- TaskEntry::cost is spend() projected.\n- task.update_budget reads UpdateOutcome, including the Suspend arm the handler currently cannot compute (it now has committed spend). Lowering below committed spend parks with committed partial evidence + continuation (B18), never truncates.\n- Committed partial evidence gains artifact identity: publications are NAMED, not counted, at the daemon layer, so 'committed partial evidence survives daemon restart; uncommitted partials are absent, never half-visible' becomes testable. Durability across restart coordinates with bn-3dr (daemon crash recovery) — do not duplicate its persistence work; this bone owes the identity binding and the wire surface, bn-3dr owes the restart machinery.\n- BudgetExhausted on the wire carries a continuation or the typed non_resumable_reason (verification-task schema, SD-13) — bn-1gc's first acceptance criterion, deferred to here because the wire join was outside its fence.\n\n# Constraints\n- Wire-visible changes follow the flag discipline (record F-flags, no silent protocol drift).\n- Suspension is a budget-layer fact the region layer cannot represent across teardown (bn-2gk concern 2, bn-1gc concern 3): a parked task's region is finalized, the continuation is the durable artifact, resume mints fresh (bn-12t's ratified resolution). Do not reopen that design.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] PR-6 IMPL-02 bullet annotated (delivered: ...) in START_HERE with the honest scope.\n- [ ] verification::unenforced gone; omissions derived from MeterSet.\n- [ ] task.update_budget five-arm table live on the wire, Suspend arm included, walked by a daemon-level test.\n- [ ] Committed partial evidence named by artifact identity; uncommitted partials absent, never half-visible.","kind":"task","labels":["kernel","phase-a","req:phase-a","req:pr-6","req:pr-6-impl-02"],"parent":"bn-19u","size":"m","title":"continuumd budget rewiring — TaskEntry on BudgetLedger, committed partial evidence with identity (PR-6 IMPL-02)"}	blake3:KQZvvT6jAMNEYP2ucPs2IQ3lt2p1be7einmawWc0sLc
