1785695994716955	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyuwg		item.comment	bn-2z0b	{"body":"INV-012 evidence delivered in bn-2z0b's workspace (crates/continuum-intent/tests/inv012_nonvacuity_evidence.rs, 12 tests, all new — no existing test touched).\n\nDesign: the guard already existed (Optimization::require_non_vacuity, PR-4/IMPL-08) with strong unit/adversarial coverage of the bare `Optimization` group; this bone's gap was whole-IntentContract-level evidence plus the specific mutant forms INV-012 and docs/50 name. Reused real corpus fixtures (die-hard-contract.json, replicated-register-contract.json) rather than hand-built contracts.\n\nClause -> test map:\n- \"required progress/availability behaviors\" -> positive_the_die_hard_contract_declares_a_progress_behavior_and_the_guard_accepts_it, positive_the_replicated_register_contract_declares_hard_soft_and_non_vacuity_together (decode, require_non_vacuity Ok, stable round-trip identity).\n- \"Safety by disabling the system is rejected\" -> negative_disabling_the_die_hards_only_progress_behavior_is_schema_legal_but_inv_012_rejects_it (the mutant: die-hard's one non_vacuity behavior emptied via a single bounded .replace on the fixture text; still schema-legal and decodes, require_non_vacuity now Err(NoNonVacuityObligation), message names INV-012, never a panic) and negative_a_repair_that_removes_the_progress_behavior_is_exactly_the_relation_the_fixtures_own_policy_blocks (before/after Optimization::changes reports exactly one Removed under PolicyField::NonVacuity and nothing under Optimization; the fixture's own policy.non_vacuity = \"no-removal\" verb denies that relation -- ties require_non_vacuity + changes + PolicyVerb::denies into one attack-and-block scenario).\n- boundary (must not over-reject) -> boundary_zero_hard_and_zero_soft_objectives_do_not_block_acceptance (one behavior suffices; die-hard's own shape is 0 hard/0 soft/1 non_vacuity).\n- boundary (must not over-accept, honestly reported) -> boundary_the_guard_counts_behaviors_it_does_not_judge_their_content: the three sets are opaque strings (RFC 0031, membership-only), so \"true\"/\"noop\"/\"placeholder\" discharge the obligation exactly as a genuine behavior does. Real triviality detection is plan Sec14.5's \"property mutation and hidden semantic variants\" -- Forge's territory, not this crate's.\n- \"mutation challenges\" clause -> boundary_mutation_challenges_are_forges_own_responsibility_and_not_yet_landed: mechanically pins that continuum-forge's crate doc names INV-012 but is still a PR-1/IMPL-01 scaffold (PR 29 not started), and that plan.md Sec14.5 states the non-vacuity-behaviors half and the mutation/hidden-variant half as two distinct sentences. Deferred rather than fabricated, per the bn-dw81/INV-006 evidence precedent.\n- schema-side -> schema_does_not_encode_inv_012s_non_emptiness_constraint: exact-text pin that optimization.non_vacuity carries only {items, type, uniqueItems} -- no minItems/required -- confirming enforcement is deliberately caller-invoked (INV-003) and not schema-encoded. No schema edit made (epoch-governed, out of fence).\n- anti-drift, proven non-vacuous -> the_check_is_not_vacuous (named after crates/continuum-task/tests/budget_dimensions.rs's idiom): mutates a local copy of plan.md's INV-012 sentence, PLAN_REQUIREMENTS.json's independently-generated copy of the same sentence, and the schema's non_vacuity block (adding a minItems sibling), and shows each of the three prose/schema comparisons this file relies on actually breaks -- plus the behavioral guard flips true/false between the good and vacuous fixtures.\n\nNotable concern for the record (documented, not a defect fixed here): negative_the_cross_field_checker_alone_would_accept_the_disabled_contract mechanically proves IntentContract::check's ContractVerdict carries no non-vacuity rule at all -- the die-hard fixture and its \"safety by disabling\" mutant produce the identical single W9 finding. A caller who trusts check().is_well_formed() alone, without separately invoking optimization().require_non_vacuity(), would accept a vacuous contract with no signal anything changed. This is already flagged in src/optimization.rs's own module doc as an open question against RFC 0037 (\"carries a lock over nothing\"); this bone only pins it as a mechanical, regression-proof fact rather than resolving the RFC question, since a new W-rule would be a schema/RFC-governed semantics change outside this bone's fence.\n\nDossier: plan.md's INV-012 heading annotated (delivered: bn-2z0b -- crates/continuum-intent/tests/inv012_nonvacuity_evidence.rs); traceability regenerated (active_requirements 703 -> 702); validate_dossier.py exits 0. No governance-checker tolerance change was needed.\n\nGates: cargo fmt --all --check clean; cargo clippy -p continuum-intent --all-targets --locked -D warnings clean; cargo test -p continuum-intent --locked: 144 unit + all existing integration suites unchanged and green + 12 new; full just check exit 0 (run twice, before and after the dossier regen).\n\nCommit: feat: INV-012 evidence -- non-vacuous synthesis guard (bn-2z0b), in-workspace at .maw/workspaces/bn-2z0b (4 files changed: the new test file, plan.md, PLAN_REQUIREMENTS.json, PLAN_BONE_TRACEABILITY.md). notes/plan/validation-results.json untouched. Bone left open per instructions -- not closed by this agent."}	blake3:nWGMc5ZKYUtP4pYemxJgimlu0JphUJLWUh6rsguobdM
1785696074023750	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyvAg		item.create	bn-32kpe	{"description":"# Context\nbn-2z0b's INV-012 evidence mechanically pins (crates/continuum-intent/tests/inv012_nonvacuity_evidence.rs::negative_the_cross_field_checker_alone_would_accept_the_disabled_contract) that IntentContract::check()'s five W-rules include no non-vacuity rule: the die-hard fixture and its emptied-non_vacuity mutant produce the identical single W9 finding. A caller trusting check().is_well_formed() alone accepts a 'safety by disabling' contract with no signal. src/optimization.rs's module doc already raises this against RFC 0037 ('a contract whose policy.non_vacuity is no-removal while optimization.non_vacuity is empty carries a lock over nothing').\n\n# Decision needed\nEither (a) RFC 0037 gains a W-rule making non-vacuity part of the cross-field verdict surface (semantic change; RFC correction + flag discipline; the pinning test flips), or (b) the two-call contract (check() + optimization().require_non_vacuity() by the caller with standing) is ratified as the design and RFC 0037/docs state it explicitly so no caller assumes check() covers it.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] RFC 0037 amended or corrected with the chosen disposition and the reasoning.\n- [ ] The pinning test updated to assert the chosen behavior (flip if (a); strengthened comment citing the disposition if (b)).\n- [ ] src/optimization.rs module-doc flag resolved to a citation.","kind":"task","labels":["phase-a","spec-debt","kernel"],"size":"xs","title":"RFC 0037 disposition — non-vacuity absent from the cross-field verdict surface (check() vs two-call contract)"}	blake3:VkqHylaSMRxfbsBjfPri_HeVu4ePQiyX1uXrQlI-TfA
1785696085976094	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyvQg		item.comment	bn-2z0b	{"body":"Landed @ 081401e59b6d. Lead re-verified in-workspace: continuum-intent 144 unit + all integration suites + 12 new evidence tests green, fmt/clippy clean, plan.md INV-012 heading annotation regen'd and validator pass.\n\nRATIFIED. (1) Citing rather than reimplementing the existing guard (Optimization::require_non_vacuity, PR-4/IMPL-08) — the gap really was whole-contract evidence over the real corpus fixtures, and building on die-hard/replicated-register instead of hand-built contracts makes the mutants schema-legal by construction. (2) The counts-not-judges boundary pair: the guard counts declared behaviors and does not judge their content — over-rejection would be its own INV-012 violation (the guard disabling synthesis), and the 'true'/'noop' acceptance test states the honest limit of a structural guard. (3) The mutation-challenges deferral: Forge is a PR-1 scaffold, so pinning 'not yet landed' mechanically beats fabricating evidence for a crate that does not compute. (4) schema_does_not_encode_inv_012s_non_emptiness_constraint retained as an honest anti-drift statement rather than an edit to an epoch-governed schema.\n\nCONCERN ROUTED. The check()-alone-accepts-the-disabled-contract fact (identical single W9 finding for fixture and mutant) is now bn-32kpe: RFC 0037 either gains a non-vacuity W-rule or the two-call contract is ratified and stated. The pinning test carries the question until then.\n\nINV-012 satisfied via heading annotation; coverage stays on this bone's label per the heading-category convention."}	blake3:tdXOlRaZQ6paTdytDeJzlFWScb_gQtH8ogGfDl86Lto
