1785696131983436	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyvwg		item.update	bn-32kpe	{"field":"labels","value":{"action":"add","label":"req:phase-a"}}	blake3:rdCa5YbcprE-wUl2FLVKjvd7fhQZLOWicUIiACklID4
1785696341534018	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEywAg		item.comment	bn-1aqq	{"body":"INV-002 evidence delivered in-workspace (bn-1aqq): crates/continuumd/tests/inv002_no_hidden_state_evidence.rs (4 tests, module-doc clause->test map quoting plan.md:311 and RFC 0026's \"No session state\"/\"Nothing is session-scoped\" clauses). Commit 38b81a9, \"feat: INV-002 evidence — explicit handles, no hidden semantic state (bn-1aqq)\".\n\nDesign: Daemon bundles one connection's Services (negotiated version/encoding, presented capability) with the whole of DaemonState 1:1 in this crate's scaffold (Server owns one Daemon by value; dispatch takes &mut self so requests never interleave). A dropped-connection/reconnect has no smaller unit to act on than the whole Daemon, so the guard's `reconnect()` helper moves DaemonState — and only DaemonState — out of the old connection's Daemon into a freshly, independently negotiated one presenting a different capability (cap_runner instead of cap_root). `store`/`store_audit` (ReferenceStore) are deliberately not carried: TaskFamily and VerificationFamily take them as `_store` (unused) in src, so every post-reconnect step (task.update_budget, task.resume, verification.result) provably never consults them — only the one workspace.create this file issues, entirely pre-drop, does.\n\n- Positive: a Die Hard campaign parked at states:4 (deterministic park point already proven in daemon_task_operations.rs) is finished two ways — one continuous connection vs. dropped-and-reconnected — and task.update_budget/task.resume/verification.result produce byte-identical wire frames (envelope + typed payload, both re-encoded via codec::to_bytes/encode_payload) either way, reaching SemanticVerdict::Refuted (Die Hard's frozen fact).\n- Negative/anti-vacuity: a look-alike daemon built with the identical deterministic setup (same intent, same sealed workspace — no outside difference) but which never itself ran verification.start denies (CapabilityDenied) the identical task/continuation handles the honest reconnect admits. This is the concrete \"hypothetical connection-scoped semantic value\" the task table would be if it lived outside DaemonState; contrasting admitted-vs-denied on the same request proves the positive test's byte-identical comparison is a real guard, not one that would pass regardless. I additionally sanity-checked this by hand: temporarily breaking `reconnect()` to discard state (a fresh DaemonState instead of the transplant) flips both the positive test and the negative test's \"honest reconnect\" arm to fail immediately, confirming detection before reverting.\n- Boundary x2: PinnedEpochs (daemon/task.rs) structurally excludes the protocol epoch (no field for it), so two EpochSets differing only in protocol produce equal PinnedEpochs; and admissible_epochs never refuses a resume for a protocol-only disagreement (RFC 0026: \"A daemon MUST NOT reject a resume with ContinuationEpochMismatch for a protocol-minor difference\") while still refusing a real semantic-epoch one (embedded anti-vacuity: same function, ContinuationEpochMismatch on the real disagreement).\n\nNo src changes — no seam was missing. Dossier: plan.md INV-002 heading now carries `(delivered: bn-1aqq — crates/continuumd/tests/inv002_no_hidden_state_evidence.rs)`; regenerated traceability moves INV-002 active->satisfied (active requirements 702->701); notes/plan/validation-results.json untouched; no governance-checker tolerance needed (all three governance checkers, boundaries, and kernel covenant passed unmodified).\n\nGates, all in-workspace: cargo fmt --all --check clean; cargo clippy -p continuumd --all-targets --locked -D warnings clean; cargo test -p continuumd --locked: 225 tests across 17 binaries (14 tests/*.rs incl. the new file + unittests + doctests), all passing, none of the pre-existing 221 changed; full `just check` (fmt-check, lint over the whole workspace, workspace test, crate boundaries, kernel covenant, governance x3, dossier validate, Lean build+axiom-manifest check) exits 0.\n\nOne cosmetic note: the commit message says \"229 tests\" where the accurate count is 225 (a miscount on my part when drafting the message) — not worth a follow-up commit for a message-only typo, flagging it here for the record.\n\nNo open concerns beyond that typo."}	blake3:uf-8eO5jZ01TeD5rbD2eUSKQVtZFjTyEdJFPMQPPDd4
1785696400634570	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEywQg		item.comment	bn-1aqq	{"body":"Landed @ 79cb12bb1875. Lead re-verified in-workspace post-rebase: 225 continuumd tests green (221 pre-existing unchanged + 4 new), fmt/clippy clean, regen idempotent, validator pass.\n\nRATIFIED. (1) The reconnect() design — moving DaemonState and ONLY DaemonState into a freshly negotiated Daemon presenting a DIFFERENT capability is the honest spelling of 'dropped connection does not change meaning': meaning rides the state the handles index, and the deliberately-different negotiation proves connection identity contributes nothing. (2) The lookalike-daemon negative as the mutant: a daemon with identical deterministic setup that never ran the campaign denies the resume the honest reconnect admits — that is 'the task table as connection-scoped hidden state' made concrete, and the hand-verified break-then-revert of reconnect() (both arms failed as expected) is the anti-vacuity proof the brief asked for. (3) The boundary pair: protocol epoch structurally absent from PinnedEpochs (RFC 0026 — connection-scoped, consumed by no task) and admissible_epochs never refusing on protocol-only disagreement while still refusing a real semantic-epoch one — the honest statement of what IS legitimately connection-scoped and why it is not semantic state. (4) No src changes needed — the architecture already held; this bone makes it a permanent regression.\n\nCommit-message '229 tests' typo noted (actual 225); accepted as cosmetic per no-amend.\n\nINV-002 satisfied via heading annotation; coverage stays on this bone's label per the heading-category convention."}	blake3:NxS5lOiDkJjs3GjTs80KMlGGqKbcmFNwTWoWPz7FrVo
1785696400670077	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEywgg		item.move	bn-1aqq	{"state":"done"}	blake3:nd8W68CT9smGyyUa1Vz0CgiJDhhKgh2ecUYjcDITb2c
1785696499821864	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEywwg		item.comment	bn-2zy	{"body":"## GREEN-AND-FLIPPED — DX-14 to Evidence. No falsification; no src semantics changed.\n\nCommits in `.maw/workspaces/bn-2zy/`: `268dc0d` (feat: campaign) and `6b71886` (chore: flip).\n\n### Instrumented phases per shape\n\nThe four lanes are **publication/suspension profiles**, not engines, and both files say so\nup front. The substitution is sound for a checkable reason: `RegionTree::cancel_outcome` is\na function of committed evidence and declared resumability **and of nothing else**, so a\nprofile presents everything the rule can see. Each lane carries its own SD-12 dimension per\ndocs/25 (`states`/`solver_ms`/`proof_ms`/`candidates`) plus a declared-and-unmetered\n`wall_ms` ceiling, so every partial result drags its INV-007 omission along. A phase is\n\"cancellation arrived after the first k beats\" — 27 in all:\n\n- **dpor** (6 beats, resumable): admitted, exploring, frontier-staged, frontier-committed,\n  next-frontier-staged, next-frontier-committed, parked-at-frontier.\n- **solver** (4 beats, **non-resumable**, `solver-state-not-exportable`): admitted,\n  querying, answer-staged, answer-committed, answered. `answer-staged` is the load-bearing\n  row: a cancelled atomic query must publish nothing.\n- **proof** (8 beats, resumable): admitted, searching, lemma-staged, lemma-committed,\n  parked-between-lemmas, resumed, next-lemma-staged, next-lemma-committed, checked — the\n  only lane making `Suspended → Running → Suspended` reachable.\n- **synthesis** (5 beats, resumable): admitted, enumerating, candidate-staged,\n  candidate-committed, next-candidate-staged, exhausted — the only lane where a *failure*\n  rather than a cancellation resolves a staged artifact.\n\nDaemon grain: 10 dispatch phases across the same four shapes (four **distinct targets**,\nbecause a `task_*` handle is the content identity of the request tuple and two lanes on one\ntarget under one budget are silently one task), plus a faulted-dispatch and an unheld-task\nphase.\n\n### Matrix dimensions and run counts\n\n`crates/continuum-task/tests/dx14_cancellation_matrix.rs` — 10 tests:\ndeclared table 27 phases × 4 placements × 3 arrivals = **324**; request window (work keeps\nstepping past the request) 27 × 4 = **108**; no-work-enters-after-request 27 × 2 = **54**;\nfour-lane portfolio in a 3-level tree, 630 interleavings × 8 injection positions = **5,040**.\nPlacements cross 0/1/1/2 region boundaries; arrivals are request/drain/teardown-in-place and\nare **required to agree**, which makes \"the outcome is a function of the phase, not of how\nfar the teardown got first\" an assertion.\n\n`crates/continuumd/tests/dx14_cancellation_matrix.rs` — 7 tests: the 10-row dispatch matrix\n(each row cancelled twice for monotonicity), no-work-after-cancel, only-work-opens-a-scope,\nthe faulted-dispatch row, the unheld-task denial, a four-lane one-daemon portfolio, and a\ntwo-run byte-identity render.\n\nEvery run is checked **four ways**: balanced obligation ledger (report *and* tree, set and\ncounters); no artifact neither committed nor absent (re-derived from the tree);\n`EvidenceBook::reconcile`'s independent third accounting from checkpoints and headroom; and\nRFC 0026 both-or-neither on every arm of every worker.\n\n### Flipped, not falsified\n\nStatus → `Evidence (reference implementation)`; Evidence column names both files with run\ncounts and mutation results; Decision column states scope (profiles-not-engines,\nmid-publication proved at calculus grain only, asupersync still Phase B / PR 14). plan §0.3\nupdated — DX-14 joins the evidence set, DX-10 alone remains open and freeze-blocking.\n`PLAN_REQUIREMENTS.json` regenerated. `validation-results.json` untouched; START_HERE\nbullets not annotated (bn-1n6r's).\n\n### Anti-vacuity guards\n\nExact run-count assertions on every sweep; all three `CancelOutcome` arms required — by the\nphase matrix *and* separately by the portfolio — plus all three terminal statuses; the\nportfolio's distinct renders must number >1 and each must contain\n`total: orphans=0 unresolved=0 balanced=true`; the request window must actually get a beat in\npast the request somewhere; `ledger.opened() > 0` and `worker_count() > 0` everywhere; the\nforbidden state is entered and *observed* (provisional flag, outstanding\n`provisional-publication:wN`, held `bytes` headroom before the drain — all absent after);\nand both conjuncts are shown able to fail (finalize-before-drain refused naming the worker;\nan unreleased reservation caught as `DanglingReservation` while the region layer reports\ntotality, so agreement is evidence rather than tautology).\n\n### Mutation testing — the campaign has teeth\n\nFive mutations applied to `src/` and reverted:\n1. `drain` stops discarding the staged publication → caught by 5 tests.\n2. `cancel_outcome` reports every committed lane resumable → caught by 4.\n3. `finalize`/`drain` accept *quiescent* not *terminal* (a parked worker survives) → 4.\n4. `Residual::admit` stops replaying committed evidence into the cancel scope → 3 daemon tests.\n5. `region::scoped` stops settling on the `Fault` path → **initially survived**; I added\n   `positive_a_run_that_faulted_leaves_a_cancellable_task_and_no_open_scope` and re-ran the\n   mutation to confirm it is now caught. That row is also the fifth residual profile\n   (`created`: nothing published, no continuation) no lane program reaches.\n\nOne mutation **survived and must not be \"fixed\"**: replacing `task.cancel`'s\n`settlement.continuation().and(entry.continuation.clone())` with a bare\n`entry.continuation.clone()` changes nothing reachable. That is correct and already\ndocumented — `task.rs`'s own `debug_assert_eq!` asserts the two readings always agree, and\n`continuation.is_some() ⇒ publications > 0` (stated on `TaskEntry::publications`) is why.\nThe join is defensive, not load-bearing. Recorded so nobody later \"simplifies\" it on the\nstrength of a green suite.\n\n### Test counts and gates\n\n`continuum-task` 141 passing (was 131, +10). `continuumd` 228 passing (was 221, +7). No\nexisting test touched. `cargo fmt --all --check` clean; `cargo clippy --all-targets --locked\n-- -D warnings` clean; **`just check` exit 0** on the committed tree (dossier validate and\nLean gate included); working tree clean.\n\n### Concerns for the lead\n\n1. **One checker tolerance widened, minimally and visibly.** `validate_dossier.py`'s §0.3\n   open-set regex became `(?:are|is) open and freeze-blocking`. Item list, sentence order and\n   equality-against-the-matrix untouched — only the verb, because English will not keep a\n   plural for a one-item list now that DX-10 is alone there.\n2. **Scope of the flip.** Closed over lifecycle *profiles*, not four engines; the argument\n   rests on `cancel_outcome` depending on exactly two facts. When a real engine lands, hold\n   it to this table. If any of them needs a *third* fact, the row needs re-examination.\n3. **Mid-publication cancellation is calculus-grain only** — no wire cancel can land between\n   a stage and its commit while `Daemon::dispatch` holds `&mut DaemonState` for a whole call.\n   Both halves say so where it bites; reachable when PR 14's asupersync adapter lands.\n4. **Portfolio sweep is 3× the established ceiling** (5,040 vs `region_no_orphan.rs`'s 1,680)\n   — same order, whole file runs in 0.1 s. Say the word and I trim to a 2,2,1,1 split (1,260).\n5. **Bone brief said continuumd was 240 across 16 suites**; this workspace's pre-existing\n   count at `3f303c5` is 221 across 14. Flagging rather than reconciling — the invariant that\n   matters (no pre-existing test changed or broke) holds.\n6. **Two doc-only edits outside `tests/`**: `region.rs`'s \"what is deferred\" bullet said \"The\n   row stays open\", which would have become false; `region_cancellation.rs` gained a pointer\n   to where the campaign landed. No code changed."}	blake3:E2mZ4iVtG1CXrtIuZ_vIhKvZ_NYiI91N4ImXdJD0qVs
1785696654300364	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyxAg		item.comment	bn-2zy	{"body":"Landed @ 423ad0c4893f. Lead re-verified post-sync in-workspace: all 27 suites across continuum-task+continuumd green (373 tests, 0 failures), fmt/clippy clean, regen idempotent.\n\nGREEN-AND-FLIPPED ACCEPTED — G0-DX-14 to Evidence (reference implementation). The flip's legitimacy rests on the argument the matrix row now states: CancelOutcome is a function of committed evidence and declared resumability AND OF NOTHING ELSE, so a publication/suspension profile presents everything the rule can see, and a real DPOR/solver/proof/synthesis engine is held to this table rather than to a new one. Concern 2 recorded as the reopening condition: an engine whose cancel behavior needs a third fact reopens the row.\n\nRATIFIED. (1) The validator verb-widening (are→(?:are|is)) — glanced as requested: grammar-only, the item list/sentence order/set-equality against the matrix untouched; exactly the extend-tolerance-without-weakening discipline. (2) The mutation campaign's discipline: the fifth mutation (scoped not settling on Fault) initially surviving and getting a fault-path ROW rather than a shrug is the point of mutation testing; 4/5 caught by multiple tests. (3) The surviving mutation's disposition: task.cancel's continuation join is defensive-not-load-bearing (source's own debug_assert + continuation.is_some() implies publications>0) — accepted, must NOT be patched into load-bearingness. (4) Portfolio sweep at 5,040 runs/0.1s — no trim; construction is linear and runtime trivial. (5) region.rs doc correction ('The row stays open' would have gone false) — doc-only, nothing in the module changed to make the campaign pass, verified by diff.\n\nSCOPE RECORDED. Mid-publication cancellation proved at calculus grain only — Daemon::dispatch holds &mut DaemonState for a whole call, so no wire cancel lands between stage and commit; the asupersync substrate (PR 14, Phase B) is where that window opens and the calculus rows are the table it will be held to. Brief's '240 tests/16 suites' was the lead's miscount; agent's flag correct (221/14 at dispatch epoch).\n\nDX-10 (ACI benchmark, PR 10) is now the SOLE open freeze-blocking G0 item."}	blake3:MtTbbt_-XYHG4mGFoquUs5mh-ui_QeKzS-_PEdI6CKs
