1785711897433354	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEysAk		item.comment	bn-2c0a	{"body":"G0-DX-10 falsification delivered (1/3) — THE ATTACK CATALOGUE. Thirteen attacks, four controls, 17 tests, all green. 8 LANDED, 4 HELD, 1 INCONCLUSIVE.\n\nHOUSE RULE. Daemon and protocol frozen (continuumd and below, untouched). The INSTRUMENT is the system under test, so variants are added BESIDE the landed metrics, never instead: ShellSurface::new is still Renderer::Standard under Disciplines::ALL, HiddenCost enters no interface-byte total, and the sensitivity table's first row is bn-134i's artifact under its own name. control_every_landed_number_is_unchanged_by_this_campaign holds all five landed figures (10,859 / 4,118 / -163% / 69permille / 69permille / 24-24 / 1000permille recovery); control_the_hidden_ledger_never_enters_an_interface_byte_total holds the instrumentation outside the measurement and shows the equality is non-vacuous; control_a_decomposed_answer_re_encodes_to_the_frame_that_carried_it holds all 172 decompositions to real frame lengths.\n\nPRO-SHELL-BIAS — is the measured native LOSS an artefact?\nS1 LANDED. The CLI's own frames are uncharged: 243,902 bytes under 172 invocations, 2.5x everything the agent read. Charging them: shell 4,118 -> 14,280 bytes/solved, margin -163% -> +23%. Still short of the +30% floor.\nS2 LANDED, and it flips a ratified margin. No handshake is charged per CLI process (875 B x 172; a CLI is one process per command and RFC 0026 gives it no session to reuse). Charging it: shell 20,551, margin +47% — CLEARS the byte floor.\nS3 LANDED, small. The expansion command is answered from an envelope the harness is still holding — no process, no frame, no handshake. 28 expansions. Fully symmetric: shell 23,245, +53%.\nS4 LANDED. The adapter renders from the very answer the daemon just produced; a real CLI re-derives state and can be a beat behind. ONE stale rendering at command 2: shell solves 20/24, invalid rate 69 -> 571permille, and the SUCCESS (+167permille) and INVALID-ACTION (87%) margins BOTH clear. Position-dependent and reported as such — stale at command 3 or 4 costs nothing, because the datum is re-read anyway. The four failures are honest (Stuck, not a wrong number). The rate is unmeasurable here and is not declared.\nS5 LANDED. One shared policy fixes the mistake count by construction — which also means only mistakes BOTH surfaces can express are ever counted. The text surface carries 25 misnameable argument positions across its eight commands; one misnamed flag costs an attempt, an invalid operation and 265 bytes at the CLI's own argument parser. The typed surface carries zero, because an argument name is a struct field and there is no call through which a caller can offer a different one. Break-even: 0.6 shell-only invalid attempts per run clears the ratified 50% reduction. At 1/run the reduction is 62%.\nS6 LANDED on the explanation, HELD on the conclusion. 172 answers re-encoded field by field. bn-23gm's stated cause is partly WRONG: next_operations costs ZERO bytes (this daemon populates none — the same producer gap Error.recovery has, which bn-1udt recorded) and the envelope-level Cost costs ZERO (the spend an agent reads is TaskRecord.cost, inside the payload). The real overhead is artifacts 20,732, omissions 16,656, assurance 15,720, epochs 8,084, plus SnapshotComponents 17,208 on the request side. Only epochs is both required and constant per connection, so it is the only conformance cost a redesign amortizes without dropping a guarantee.\nS7 HELD. research/25 declares no alternative counting rule. Every bytes/k rule is affine with the same divisor on both arms, so k in {3,4,5,8} all give exactly -163%. The one non-affine rule tried — words and punctuation counted separately, under which canonical JSON costs 309 tokens per 1000 bytes against the projection's 145 — gives -461%, further AGAINST the typed arm. No counting rule available to this campaign improves the typed arm's position.\n\nPRO-NATIVE-BIAS — are the claimed typed ADVANTAGES artefacts?\nN1 HELD. zero_cost_invalid is honest and correctly scoped. Priced at the 411-byte request frame the client would have written, the 4 locally refused calls are worth 69 bytes per solved task: -163% -> -165%. The rate is unchanged, which is the anti-cheating rule holding — they were already counted invalid.\nN2 LANDED. Every injected fault lands on both arms by construction; there is a class that structurally cannot. Renaming ONE projected key (cost.states, verdict, or task) takes the baseline from 24/24 to 0/24 with the typed arm untouched; success margin 0 -> +1000permille. The disciplined baseline fails HONESTLY — all 24 runs stop at Stuck::UnreadableAnswer rather than report a number they could not read — and the undisciplined one fails at 923permille invalid. No typed analogue exists: a field name belongs to the schema and a schema change is a protocol version.\nN3 LANDED. Discipline 1 carries the ENTIRE baseline: without anchored key lookup it solves 0/24 at 923permille invalid, because a lookup for 'task' finds the task.status line. Disciplines 2 and 4 are INERT on the standard projection — dropping either changes not one byte of the artifact — and are load-bearing only under the injected renderers (Flaky for 4, Drifting for 2). Discipline 3 is a pure 119 bytes/solved-task cost. This also supplies RFC 0027's missing first ablation rung, which the instrument does not run: against a RAW shell agent the typed arm wins success by +1000permille and invalid-action rate by 92%.\nN4 HELD. All four leave-one-out subsets still pass the plan 19.4 separation check (so each is a subset a result could legitimately be reported over) and reproduce every conclusion: byte margin -163/-163/-164/-164%, success 0, invalid reduction 0. No landed conclusion depends on which task is in the set.\nN5 HELD, and it points the other way. Dropping the ceiling_enforced clause from the completion criterion leaves BOTH arms at 24/24; its only effect is the 119 bytes/solved task the baseline pays for the expansion, and removing it WIDENS the typed arm's loss to -171%. The instrument's single deliberate concession to the typed arm is real, small, and not holding the result up.\n\nX1 INCONCLUSIVE, with its reason typed per INV-008's spirit: the governing text does not decide it. RFC 0027 fixes the metric and the denominator ('interface bytes per solved task') and never says WHOSE interface. Under the agent's stdin/stdout the margin is -163%; under total protocol traffic it is +53%. Both readings are defensible from the text as written, and that one undecided choice decides the byte metric's sign."}	blake3:2MMm_K6HafruOsHkvuwH4PYS-n6E5Btc9B9c_gmZy3U
1785711922742090	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEysQk		item.comment	bn-2c0a	{"body":"G0-DX-10 falsification (2/3) — THE SENSITIVITY TABLE AND THE SURVIVING CONCLUSIONS.\n\nSENSITIVITY TABLE. Native / shell interface bytes per solved task, byte margin, and which of the three ratified margins clears (success:bytes:invalid). Row 1 is the landed artifact under its own name, so a reader cannot quote a variant thinking it is the measurement.\n\n  landed                         10859 / 4118    -163%   f:f:f\n  cli-frames                     10859 / 14280    +23%   f:f:f\n  cli-frames+handshakes          10859 / 20551    +47%   f:T:f\n  symmetric                      10859 / 23245    +53%   f:T:f\n  composed-refusals-priced       10928 / 4118    -165%   f:f:f\n  symmetric-both-ways            10928 / 23245    +52%   f:T:f\n  stale-read-at-command-2        10859 / 4052    -167%   T:f:T   shell 20/24, 571permille\n  projection-key-renamed         10859 / none    undef   T:f:f   shell 0/24\n  raw-shell-baseline             10859 / none    undef   T:f:T   shell 0/24, 923permille\n  baseline-without-expansion     10859 / 3999    -171%   f:f:f\n  shell-only-mistakes-1-per-run  10859 / 4383    -147%   f:f:T   invalid reduction 62%\n  without-dh-all                 10849 / 4123    -163%   f:f:f\n  without-dh-type-ok             10850 / 4125    -163%   f:f:f\n  without-dp-all                 10866 / 4108    -164%   f:f:f\n  without-dp-ownership           10872 / 4115    -164%   f:f:f\n\nNO ROW makes all three margins clear simultaneously. That is asserted, and it is the sentence aci-benchmark-margins actually asks about ('missing any one of the three margins fails G0-DX-10').\n\nENVELOPE DECOMPOSITION — the redesign-actionable half. 172 answers, 170,584 result bytes, 73,318 request bytes, floor 109,392.\n  artifacts        conformance-varying   20732\n  omissions        conformance-varying   16656\n  assurance        conformance-varying   15720\n  epochs           conformance-CONSTANT   8084\n  cost             conformance-varying       0\n  warnings         conformance-varying       0\n  next_operations  amortizable               0\n  SnapshotComponents (request side)      17208 over 24 workspace.create requests\n  redesign_reducible 25292   maximal_reducible 78400\n\nSURVIVING CONCLUSIONS — what an adjudicator may rely on, whichever way each attacked choice is decided.\n\n1. SUCCESS is a TIE, and it is the most robust result in the lane. 24/24 both arms under every accounting variant, every leave-one-out subset, and both policies. The +10pp floor is met ONLY where the baseline is degraded — a raw undisciplined scraper, a drifted projection, or a stale read — never where the typed arm improves.\n\n2. INVALID-ACTION RATE is a TIE at 69/69permille, stable under every accounting variant and every task subset — but the tie is an artefact of the POLICY, not a property of the two surfaces. The shared policy can only make mistakes both surfaces can express, and 0.6 shell-only invalid attempts per run clears the ratified 50% reduction. The tie is a LOWER BOUND on the typed arm's advantage, not a measurement of it.\n\n3. BYTES: the SIGN of the margin is decided by an accounting choice the governing text leaves open (X1). Agent stdin/stdout -163%; CLI frames charged +23%; frames and per-invocation handshakes +47%; fully symmetric +53%. The +30% floor is missed under the landed rule and cleared under symmetric connection accounting.\n\n4. BYTES, the part no accounting choice moves: under the landed rule the loss is NOT an envelope-overhead artefact. Reducing the whole result envelope to its floor AND resolving SnapshotComponents by reference still leaves the typed arm at 7,668 bytes per solved task against 4,118 — a -86% margin. A redesign of the ENCODING cannot close it. If the landed reading of 'interface bytes' is the right one, the byte failure is structural: a protocol client transmits the whole typed answer where a text projection prints the fields the agent asked about.\n\n5. RECOVERY parity (1000permille both arms) holds under every SYMMETRIC fault and is CONDITIONAL on a projection that never drifts and is never stale. One renamed key or one stale read breaks the baseline and not the typed arm; the instrument declares both rates to be zero and can measure neither.\n\n6. The instrument's own concessions are small and now measured, in both directions: the free local refusal is worth 69 bytes/solved task to the typed arm, and the omission-manifest clause in the completion criterion is worth 119 bytes/solved task to the baseline. Neither changes any verdict, and the second one widens rather than narrows the typed arm's loss.\n\n7. What no variant here can supply: a LIVE MODEL. Every conclusion above is about what ONE SCRIPTED BEHAVIOUR costs through two interfaces. research/25's own proposed mechanism for the invalid-action margin — validating a plan against the register before acting — is unexercised, and this campaign did not build it. Four tasks, two semantic families, scripted policies: every bn-2c0a variant varies the INTERFACE or the ACCOUNTING; none varies the AGENT."}	blake3:aSEDQu2dIcy5HtkQ4CR2qqcjkwK4T5oaHBPSbyyjGtc
1785711953256224	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEysgk		item.comment	bn-2c0a	{"body":"G0-DX-10 falsification (3/3) — MATRIX ROW, FILES, COMMITS, COUNTS, GATES, CONCERNS.\n\nMATRIX ROW. notes/plan/notes/G0_SPIKE_MATRIX.md, G0-DX-10. Evidence and Decision columns record the PR-10 instrument and this campaign in the DX-03/DX-14 style: the five measured metrics, the thirteen attacks with their verdicts and numbers, the envelope decomposition, and the scope. Status left EXACTLY as found — 'Open — freeze-blocking (Phase A)' — not flipped, not upgraded. The row now states plainly, against its own pass condition (higher success, lower tokens, fewer invalid actions), that the surviving numbers MEET NONE OF THE THREE under the landed accounting: success is a measured tie at 24/24, invalid-action rate a measured tie at 69/69permille, and interface bytes a 2.6x loss — and that adjudicating the row, and the redesign call its failure consequence names, is bn-762i's and is privileged to the user. The exit line is not annotated; no redesign call is made here.\n\nFILES.\n  crates/continuum-benchmark/tests/dx10_falsification.rs  NEW — the attack catalogue: 13 attacks + 4 controls, 17 tests, campaign map in the module header.\n  crates/continuum-benchmark/src/variants.rs              NEW — every landed accounting choice restated as a parameter: Accounting (6 named rules), Cell/shell_sweep with the hidden ledger, handshake_bytes, Sensitivity + row/under/plain, the envelope Decomposition, flag_names/misnamed_argument_cost, invalid_reduction_breakeven_tenths, with_shell_only_mistakes, ceiling_free_completion, leave_one_out/restrict.\n  crates/continuum-benchmark/src/falsification.rs         NEW — the typed artifact: Attack/Direction/Outcome (Landed, Held, Inconclusive-with-reason), FalsificationReport with a total byte-stable render, its own limits section.\n  crates/continuum-benchmark/src/shell.rs                 ADDITIVE ONLY — HiddenCost, Disciplines (ALL is the landed baseline), Renderer::Stale, Renderer::Drifting, Recorded, scrape_with, loose_field, drift, structural_tokens, ShellSurface::configured/recording/hidden. dispatch now reads its own frame lengths off the frames it writes and takes (behaviour identical; client_send/client_receive replaced with the explicit encode/put/take/decode they perform). Every landed constructor and every landed number unchanged.\n  crates/continuum-benchmark/src/lib.rs                   module docs for the two new modules.\n  notes/plan/notes/G0_SPIKE_MATRIX.md                     the DX-10 row.\n\nCOMMITS in workspace .maw/workspaces/bn-2c0a, not merged, not pushed:\n  135d1ce  feat: G0-DX-10 falsification — the instrument attacked from both sides (bn-2c0a)\n  1960bfa  chore: G0-DX-10 matrix row records the campaign; Status left Open for bn-762i\n\nCOUNTS. cargo test --workspace --locked: 1958 passed / 0 failed. The pristine baseline in THIS workspace is 1941, measured by stashing the campaign and re-counting — the brief's 1904 was bn-134i's pre-sync figure and is stale. So +17 exactly, all in continuum-benchmark (49 -> 66); continuum-mcp unchanged at 10. No test deleted, weakened, or ignored.\n\nGATES. cargo fmt --all --check clean. cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --locked -D warnings clean. cargo test -p continuum-benchmark -p continuum-mcp --locked green. just check exit 0 — crate boundaries, kernel covenant, five governance checkers with self-tests, dossier validate_dossier.py program_status 'ready' status 'pass', Lean 19 jobs, axiom manifest up to date. validation-results.json untouched. No .bones/ change in either commit. Checker tolerance untouched.\n\nCONCERNS, recorded rather than resolved.\n(a) X1 is the load-bearing open question and it is a TEXT question, not a measurement one. Until 'interface bytes per solved task' is read as either the agent's stdin/stdout or the whole protocol exchange, the byte margin has no sign: -163% one way, +53% the other. bn-762i should decide it EXPLICITLY rather than inherit the harness's reading by default, because inheriting it silently is how a defensible choice becomes an unexamined premise.\n(b) S4 and S5 both flip ratified margins at rates this instrument cannot measure. They establish that the two ties are LOWER BOUNDS on the typed arm's advantage; they do NOT establish that the typed arm wins. Quoting either variant as a result would be the mirror image of the error this campaign was sent to find, and the artifact's limits section says so inside the artifact.\n(c) N3 shows disciplines 2 and 4 are inert against the standard projection — dropping either changes not one byte. They are not decorations (the injected renderers fire both) but the baseline's landed numbers do not depend on them, and a reader should not take 'four disciplines' as four independent guards. crate::shell already says this about discipline 4 and did not say it about 2; it does now.\n(d) The envelope decomposition is measured on the baseline's 172 dispatches while the typed arm makes 168 wire calls (its register refuses four before the wire), and the two arms' frames differ by the 2-byte request-id length. The scaling is applied where the decomposition is used against the typed arm's totals and is stated at the line that scales it.\n(e) 'artifacts' at 20,732 bytes is the single largest envelope cost — larger than the omission manifest and larger than the assurance envelope — and this campaign did NOT investigate why a workspace.create answer carries an ArtifactRef at all. It is measured, classified conformance-varying, and left named for a redesigner rather than guessed at.\n(f) The falsification report is a second artifact beside crate::report::Report deliberately, so a variant can never be quoted as the measurement. If a future reader wants one artifact, they should merge them knowing that is the property being given up.\n\nBone left open per instruction."}	blake3:ofJUMkun172oxh4fwHesWiq8oleWypQtR7_58up4YSM
1785712075959190	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyswk		item.comment	bn-2c0a	{"body":"Landed @ 2f3066c35bf9. Lead re-verified: 1958 workspace tests green (+17 exactly over the pristine re-count), every landed bn-134i number held unchanged by the campaign's own control, matrix Status left exactly as found, no exit annotation, no redesign call — the privilege boundary respected precisely.\n\nRATIFIED. (1) The house rule — variants BESIDE landed metrics with a control asserting the landed figures unmoved — is what lets both sets of numbers be trusted at once. (2) The verdict discipline (LANDED/HELD/INCONCLUSIVE-typed) with S6's split verdict (landed on the explanation, held on the conclusion — bn-23gm's stated cause partly wrong, next_operations and Cost cost ZERO bytes; the real ledger is artifacts 20,732 / omissions 16,656 / assurance 15,720 / SnapshotComponents 17,208 / epochs 8,084). (3) The refusal to quote unmeasurable rates as results (S4/S5 flip margins at rates this instrument cannot measure — concern b is the campaign refusing to commit its own target's error). (4) The N-side symmetric rigor: zero_cost_invalid priced at composition and found nearly worthless (69 B); the discipline decomposition finding two of four inert. (5) The structural-loss decomposition: maximal encoding redesign still leaves −86% under the landed rule — the single most redesign-actionable number produced.\n\nSURVIVING CONCLUSIONS accepted as the adjudication basis: success tie robust; invalid-action tie is a POLICY ARTIFACT lower-bounding the typed advantage (25 misnameable text positions vs 0 typed; break-even 0.6 shell-only invalid attempts/run); byte-margin SIGN rests on X1, an accounting question RFC 0027's text leaves open (−163% one reading, +53% the other); no sensitivity row clears all three ratified margins simultaneously (asserted mechanically); recovery parity conditional on never-drifting projection; no live model exercised.\n\nX1 ROUTED: the reading of 'interface bytes' is a spec-text decision and lands in the bn-762i decision package to the user, NOT inherited from the harness by default (concern a adopted verbatim). artifacts-at-20,732-B left named for the redesigner (concern e).\n\nG0-DX-10 coverage stays on this bone's label until adjudication; row correctly still Open — freeze-blocking."}	blake3:dg59SgZkxzGX-9qgYJAsVnomWOmXXln27WRCtQqSBAc
