1785712128913467	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEytgk		item.comment	bn-762i	{"body":"DECISION PACKAGE — G0-DX-10 / PR-10 exit (prepared by the lead; the decision is the user's; this bone does not close until it is made).\n\nTHE QUESTION. The exit sentence: 'native ACI is measurably more effective or the protocol is redesigned before freeze.' The G0-DX-10 row's pass condition: higher success, lower tokens, fewer invalid actions. DX-10 is the SOLE remaining freeze-blocking G0 item.\n\nTHE MEASUREMENT (bn-134i instrument, held honest by the bn-2c0a two-sided falsification; every number below survived both attack directions).\n- Success: TIE, 24/24 both arms — robust under every variant. The +10pp floor is met only where the baseline is artificially degraded.\n- Invalid actions: TIE at 69 per-mille — but proven a POLICY ARTIFACT that lower-bounds the typed advantage: the shared scripted policy can only make mistakes both surfaces can express; the text surface has 25 misnameable argument positions, the typed surface 0; break-even is 0.6 shell-only invalid attempts per run, and any realistic fallible agent exceeds that.\n- Bytes/solved task: the SIGN of this margin rests on X1, an accounting question RFC 0027's text leaves open ('interface bytes per solved task' — whose interface?). Landed reading (typed arm's frames vs projected text): native 10,859 vs shell 4,118 = −163%. Symmetric reading (charge the CLI's own frames + per-process handshake): +47% to +53%, clearing the +30% floor. Both readings are defensible from the text.\n- Structural floor: under the landed reading, a MAXIMAL encoding redesign still leaves −86% (7,668 vs 4,118). The cost ledger: artifacts 20,732 B (largest, uninvestigated — named for a redesigner), omissions 16,656, assurance 15,720, SnapshotComponents-on-wire 17,208, epochs 8,084. next_operations and Cost cost ZERO (the folk explanation was wrong).\n- No sensitivity row clears all three ratified margins simultaneously (asserted mechanically).\n\nTHE OPTIONS.\n(A) DECIDE X1 = symmetric accounting, and accept the exit as 'measurably more effective' on bytes (+47%) + the artifact-argument on invalid actions, with success a tie. Honest risk: reads as choosing the accounting that flips the sign after seeing the numbers; the falsification campaign itself warns bn-762i must decide X1 explicitly ON THE TEXT, not by convenience. If chosen, RFC 0027 gets a correction pinning the reading, and the row flips with the reasoning recorded.\n(B) REDESIGN before freeze (the row's own failure consequence: 'simplify/rework ACI'). The actionable ledger above says where: artifacts, omission manifests, assurance envelope, SnapshotComponents-by-reference. A redesign is protocol-minor-plus (wire-visible everywhere) — the deferred-and-bundled bump discipline applies. The instrument re-runs mechanically after; margins re-measured.\n(C) HYBRID: decide X1 on the text (either way), AND commission the targeted slimming of the named ledger items as PR-5-follow-up work regardless — the −86% structural floor under the landed reading says the envelope carries real weight even if the accounting question goes native's way.\n(D) WIDEN THE INSTRUMENT first (live-model run or fallible-policy families per research/25's unexercised plan-validation mechanism) before deciding — accepts freeze delay; the scripted-policy limitation is the one both campaigns name.\n\nLEAD'S RECOMMENDATION, for what it is worth: (C). X1 should be decided on RFC 0027's text by the human who owns the spec's meaning; independently, the byte ledger names five concrete costs whose slimming is worth commissioning under either reading — 'artifacts 20,732 B uninvestigated' should not survive Phase A either way. I make no move until directed.\n\nEvidence trail: bn-134i/bn-23gm/bn-3awq/bn-1udt/bn-26tb (instrument + five metrics), bn-2c0a (falsification, 13 attacks + 4 controls), crates/continuum-benchmark/tests/{pr10_*,dx10_falsification}.rs, the typed report artifacts, G0_SPIKE_MATRIX.md DX-10 row (Status honestly Open — freeze-blocking)."}	blake3:AVJYCUCWUkVAodciPYw_7oHZt9DAvfEHN8RCfIE84N4
