1785866466433843	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEypgo		item.comment	bn-1dj05	{"body":"Recorded F19 in RFC 0026's flag ledger (notes/plan/rfcs/0026-continuumd-native-protocol.md, after F18, before 'Rejected alternatives'), matching the F15-F18 voice/structure. F19: Error.data has no declared schema for CertificateRejected's rejection reason. States what exists today — certificate_rejected's Fault::detail is a non-interpolated &'static str under rule envelope.no_prose, one string per kernel family naming the checker rather than the reason (crates/continuumd/src/daemon/evidence.rs:1052-1085, verified current on trunk); Error.data is absent daemon-wide because no code declares a data schema (crates/continuumd/src/daemon/result.rs:22-27, also verified current) — states what it would add (a declared Error.data schema for CertificateRejected, or a typed field, carrying the kernel's rejection reason to the wire — F19 is a second concrete proposal alongside F11's retry-after, both anchored to correction 46), and states what it waits on (not payable by this document alone; schema, codec, conformance vectors, and CLI rendering ride together when a protocol-minor bump takes it, so raised for that bundle rather than proposed here). Cites bn-dtg61's verdict-fidelity audit and bn-1dj05. No IDL/code/schema changes made — doc-only, single-line addition. Confirmed the flag was not already recorded anywhere in notes/plan before adding it. just check exits 0 (dossier validator pass, Lean build 19/19, axiom manifest clean). Committed in-workspace at 76ece7c. Bone left in doing state; not merged, not closed, not pushed."}	blake3:_xWdWVqi2FfpYgJOZxaam66Y2fLxwdTVzQfm0p1lt1o
1785866504377119	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEypwo		item.comment	bn-1dj05	{"body":"Lead: reviewed and merged @ epoch 86a9335. F19 recorded per the F15-F18 convention — framed correctly as the second concrete Error.data proposal alongside F11's retry-after (correction 46 cross-ref), with the transcribe-kernel-enums-into-statics alternative declined at source per bn-dtg61's second-authority reasoning. Both code claims re-verified against trunk before recording. Deferred-and-bundled: rides the next protocol-minor bump with schema + codec + vectors + CLI rendering together. One line, one file."}	blake3:tUzHKyHq65-A-5nxnTp3-m7r3bfK-ofqaV_Cp6cR2Hs
