1785867294294117	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyAQ		item.comment	bn-y9f7i	{"body":"Disposition: ratified, plus F20 raised. verification.start's task_started lane on a re-issued identical request against a cancelled (or otherwise non-Completed terminal) campaign identity is NOT a violation of RFC 0026's own text. Governing quotes: IDL op summary 'Returns a task handle, or a cached result when one exists for the same snapshot, intent, target, and epochs'; RFC 0026 line 185 '`@task_starting` is a *may*, not a *must*... A client MUST handle both shapes; a daemon MUST NOT fabricate a task handle to make the shape uniform'; correction 45 'a result's status lane is a fact about what the operation did; only a `@task_starting` operation may report `task_started` or `task_suspended`... `task_suspended` MUST carry both `task` and `continuation`' — a shape rule (task-shaped vs result-shaped), never an event claim that new execution began at this call. The cached-result branch is licensed only when a completed output exists to reuse (RFC 0030 reuse classes); a Cancelled/Failed task has none, so the task branch (task_started, absent a continuation) is the only well-formed answer — not a design choice defended after the fact but what the two-branch response already requires. Real asymmetry found and recorded rather than fixed: task.resume's own terminal short-circuit (daemon::task::resume, bn-10093/A1-A2) answers status=ok on the task-observing lane for the identical 'already-terminal' situation, while verification.start has no equivalent branch (its cached lane checks only TaskStatus::Completed). Mirroring that shape in verification.start would close A12 completely but flips an existing scenario's ResultStatus (task_started -> ok), a wire-visible change out of this bone's fence — recorded as F20 in RFC 0026's flag ledger for the next protocol-minor bundle. Changed: notes/plan/rfcs/0026-continuumd-native-protocol.md (new disposition subsection under 'Task lifecycle' + F20 ledger entry), crates/continuumd/src/daemon/verification.rs (doc comments on the cached-lane branch and started()), crates/continuumd/src/daemon/task.rs (doc comment on resume's terminal short-circuit, cross-referencing the disposition and F20), crates/continuumd/tests/dx14_falsification.rs (A12 doc comment updated from 'concern recorded' to 'disposed, ratified, F20 raised'; campaign-map table row updated; assertions unchanged). No behavior changes, no wire byte changes. Gates: cargo fmt --all --check exit 0; cargo clippy --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings exit 0 (no warnings); cargo test -p continuumd --locked: 28 binaries, 424 tests passed, 0 failed (dx14_falsification.rs: 13 passed including the updated A12 test); just check: exit 0 (governance, dossier, Lean all pass). Commit 3b5232e in-workspace."}	blake3:OnzwE-pC7fF6ZP66ZHzibG8a55SRb3Pv0_N2TbvaprI
