1785867345944059	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyAw		item.assign	bn-y9f7i	{"action":"assign","agent":"continuum-dev"}	blake3:EkeWbiCiu-TJwntTI6LOwsxZHLBsZhY7QSp7LpwqpwU
1785867470174359	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyrQo		item.comment	bn-y9f7i	{"body":"Lead: disposition RATIFIED and merged @ epoch 50f6834. task_started on verification.start states the answer is task-shaped, not that execution began — forced by the two-branch response shape itself (a cancelled task has no output for the result branch to reuse; RFC 0030 reuse classes), with correction 45 read correctly as a shape rule, not an event claim. The genuinely valuable find: task.resume's terminal short-circuit (bn-10093) and verification.start answer the identical already-terminal-identity fact two different ways — recorded as F20 with the minimal closing shape (entry.is_terminal() ahead of the cached/started split, observing-lane status=ok) and correctly withheld as wire-visible for the next protocol-minor bundle. A12 pin doc updated concern→disposed, assertions untouched. 424 continuumd tests green."}	blake3:p2AUUniDN7pcY3nZMvU9R-JEUuHxSmIZR3Z6R2CHC5s
