1785867569355491	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyrwo		item.comment	bn-1g7e4	{"body":"PR-13 second command group landed in .maw/workspaces/bn-1g7e4 (commit 46ca759).\n\nWHAT LANDED (crates/continuum-cli)\n- New modules src/{evidence,debug,repair}.rs; wire.rs gains evidence_get + debug_open/debug_state/repair_begin/repair_review over a new generic Connection::invoke_typed (context_expand refactored onto it, classify_context -> generic classify_typed); render.rs gains the shared Projection/project, the Depth type, and embedded()/embedded_bytes() for Opaque fields; cli.rs gains the debug/repair/evidence noun groups and a BOOLEAN_FLAGS table (--json, --inline).\n- Commands: 'continuum evidence show <ev_*> [--inline]' (evidence.get, LIVE); 'continuum debug open <artifact> [--observer]' (debug.open); 'continuum debug state <dbg_*> [--observer]' (debug.state); 'continuum repair begin <crash_*> --gate-profile <profile>' (repair.begin); 'continuum repair review <rt_*>' (repair.review).\n- SPELLING NOTE for the lead: the plan line writes 'continuum debug' / 'continuum repair' bare. Both need a verb to pick among 11 debug and 8 repair operations, and cli-conventions.md is noun-then-verb, so they shipped as two verbs each. Flag if the lead wants the bare spellings aliased.\n\nINV-002: every command takes its handles positionally on every invocation. No session file, no current task/branch/transaction/node, Connection holds none. That is why debug is two verbs rather than one that opens a branch and remembers it — 'debug open' prints the dbg_* in full and 'debug state' takes one back.\n\nTYPED-UNSUPPORTED DEPTHS AND THE WIRE GAPS THEY WAIT ON\nrender::Depth is {served, unsupported, refused}, DERIVED from the daemon's own ErrorCode (UnsupportedSemanticFeature => unsupported), never from a hard-coded list in the CLI — the day a family registers, the same code prints 'served' with no edit. Every format prints 'operation <name>' and 'depth <token>' on both arms, so the answer names exactly which surface is unsupported. Exit 1 (a refusal), never a crash, never exit 2; JSON carries every response key present-and-null so nothing is fabricated.\n- debug.open, debug.state: UNSUPPORTED. continuumd registers all 11 debug rows and declares every request/response struct (protocol/operations/debug.rs) but has NO debug OperationFamily and NO daemon::family::Arguments arm, so codec::operations::decode_arguments answers UnknownOperation => UnsupportedSemanticFeature before dispatch. Waits on PR 19.\n- repair.begin, repair.review: UNSUPPORTED, identically. All 8 repair rows registered, structs declared, no family, no Arguments arm. Waits on PR 20.\n- evidence.get: SERVED by daemon::evidence::EvidenceFamily. Success, RFC 0027 X2 denial (CapabilityDenied, no not-found oracle — asserted), RFC 0026 Redacted stub beside the record and beside the redaction omission, and the typed 'unsupported' omission naming evidence.inline_content that an --inline request earns, all driven live.\nFrames are always really sent — nothing short-circuits — so the unsupported answer is the daemon's, not the CLI's guess. Same reading bn-3tz60 gave context.expand before bn-28jj.\n\nNO PROTOCOL CHANGES: no operation, field, or rule added, renamed, or modified; the 72-row registry and the 28 landed Arguments/Payload variants are untouched. NO NEW DEPENDENCIES — dependency-rationale.toml needs no entry.\n\nTESTS: tests/evidence_show.rs (6, live daemon) and tests/debug_repair_surface.rs (18, real Server/LocalPair with no families registered, plus renderer-first success arms proven against the real wire types ahead of PR 19/20), plus 8 new unit tests in cli.rs/render.rs. Golden pins are byte-for-byte on the debug.open unsupported JSON, the evidence.get denial JSON, and line-for-line on the debug.open and repair.review unsupported text; pretty is proven to differ from text by exactly one line and to remove nothing. Adversarial input is linear (one 64 KiB repeat, echoed back untruncated).\nCOUNTS: continuum-cli 26 -> 57 tests. Workspace 2,272 -> 2,304. cargo fmt --all --check, cargo clippy --all-targets --locked -D warnings, cargo test -p continuum-cli --locked, and full 'just check' all exit 0."}	blake3:cc_MZm-ZpWPJYVzVPwHdX4oaiJMX16f9yHxv8ldeyjE
1785867650412585	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEysAo		item.comment	bn-1g7e4	{"body":"Lead: reviewed and merged @ epoch 45608e7. Ratifications: (1) noun-then-verb spelling (debug open/state, repair begin/review) RATIFIED over the plan's bare spellings — cli-conventions.md governs and the plan is a map, not the spec; no aliases now, revisit if the G8 study surfaces demand. (2) --gate-profile required-not-defaulted RATIFIED — the vocabulary's 'default' member is a profile NAME, and the CLI silently choosing which gates a repair is held to would be a policy decision it has no standing to make. (3) The Depth design is the right shape: derived from the daemon's own ErrorCode with frames really sent (no client-side list to rot), exhaustive test pins UnsupportedSemanticFeature as the ONLY unsupported reading. (4) Admitted-carries-no-verdict noted as a PR-19/20 rider: when debug.open/repair.review go live, StructuralVerdictValue/PolicyVerdictValue rendering joins the family bones — recorded here so it isn't rediscovered. evidence show live via evidence.get; X2 no-existence-oracle denial pinned. continuum-cli 26→57, workspace 2,304 tests."}	blake3:G4yspRSYhDJ4ERQmUQy6-ko2tz16IJRjiIdo66XZu4g
