1785872415289213	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy2Qo		item.create	bn-3jrtz	{"description":"The deferred-and-bundled protocol-minor discipline (executed for 3.0→3.1, 3.1→3.2, 3.2→3.3) accumulates wire-visible candidates until a bump pays them together — schema, codec, conformance vectors, and CLI rendering riding as one unit. Current ledger candidates: RFC 0026 F19 (a declared Error.data schema for CertificateRejected carrying the kernel's rejection reason; bn-1dj05/bn-dtg61), RFC 0026 F20 (verification.start gains task.resume's terminal short-circuit shape — entry.is_terminal() ahead of the cached/started split answering status=ok on the observing lane; flips a reachable scenario's ResultStatus, bn-y9f7i/bn-3p32 A12), RFC 0028 F13 (omissions[].kind free string → closed SelectionKind enum, mirroring the F5/correction-2 precedent for expansions[].relation; bn-6ekf7). Sweep both RFC flag ledgers for any further riders at execution time. This is the PHASE-A-DEL-02 (native daemon protocol) carrier bone: the protocol deliverable's remaining known work is exactly this bundle. Execution is lead-gated: the bump decision follows the ratified deferred-and-bundled standing decision; scope additions beyond recorded flags need fresh ratification.","kind":"task","title":"Next protocol-minor bundle: F19 CertificateRejected Error.data, F20 verification.start terminal short-circuit, RFC 0028 F13 omissions[].kind enum"}	blake3:mlN-OAJka0k_QMpVVyuH5aAz7O8lsWlWnPPURk2PByE
