1785873502388930	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy4go		item.comment	bn-2w2s	{"body":"PR-11 / IMPL-05 \"replay reference\" delivered.\n\n**What `replay` honestly is.** It is not a `selected[].kind` member — RFC 0028 spells the eleven `selected[].kind` members exhaustively in \"Selection and the causal core\" (`event`, `state_delta`, `source`, `model`, `proof`, `assumption`, `counterfactual`, `obligation_flow`, `order_constraint`, `repair_surface`, `unknown`) and `replay` is not among them. It is a **top-level pack field**, required and nullable: `context-pack.schema.json` `properties.replay` types it as `^crash_[A-Za-z0-9_-]+$` or `null`, and RFC 0028's \"Required fields\" table's \"exact replay and debugger handles\" row confirms it: \"`replay`, `debugger_branch` | `^crash_` nullable; `^dbg_` nullable | `replay` MUST be non-null whenever `ReplayPreserving` is claimed.\" So `ReplayRef` does not gain an `into_selected_item` the way IMPL-03's `SourceRef`/`ModelActionRef` do — there is no `SelectionKind::Replay` and none was added, on the closed-enum discipline `selection.rs` already states for itself.\n\n**Payload, read minimally.** The schema names one shape for `replay` and no other: a class-checked `crash_*` handle. `ReplayRef::new(ArtifactHandle) -> Result<Self, ReplayRefError>` refuses every class but `ArtifactClass::Crashpack`, on the `ModelActionRef::with_model` pattern exactly. Two adjacent texts could have widened this and are both read and declined explicitly in the module doc: `continuum-engine-reference`'s witness module (`crates/continuum-engine-reference/src/witness.rs`), which produces \"a sequence of `(action, state)` pairs\" — that's the crashpack's own content, not the pack's handle to it; and `crashpack.schema.json` itself, which happens to declare a *different*, nested field also spelled `replay` (a `{command, working_directory, environment, choice_log, expected_verdict}` reproduction recipe, one schema layer down inside the artifact `crash_*` names) — a different schema reusing this bullet's word by coincidence, not a second shape for the context pack's own `replay`.\n\n**INV-016 / declined scope.** This crate cannot mint the handle it references: \"nothing in this workspace builds a crashpack\" (`crates/continuumd/src/daemon/task.rs`), so `ReplayRef::new` accepts an already-minted handle and class-checks it — accept-when-given, stated, same as `ModelActionRef::with_model` for `model_*`. Also declined, honestly: the cross-field rule that `replay` MUST be non-null whenever `ReplayPreserving` is claimed (C2) or whenever the pack is a failure profile — both are statements about a whole pack's other fields (`guarantees`, `verdict`), which this module doesn't have; that's pack assembly's job, no single IMPL bullet's fence, same reasoning `selection.rs` gives for declining per-item content identity. Running the replay (INV-006's checker) is `continuum-engine-reference`'s job, not a reference type's — `ReplayRef` names the crashpack, it does not open it. `debugger_branch` (`dbg_*`), named in the same required-fields row, belongs to RFC 0029's debugger and no PR-11 bullet claims it.\n\n**Files (in-workspace only):**\n- `crates/continuum-context/src/replay.rs` (new) — `ReplayRef`, `ReplayRefError`\n- `crates/continuum-context/tests/pr11_impl05_replay_reference.rs` (new) — 6 tests\n- `crates/continuum-context/src/lib.rs` — one `pub mod replay;` line + one doc-sentence module entry, no reflow\n- `notes/plan/notes/START_HERE_IMPLEMENTATION.md` — bullet annotated\n- `notes/plan/notes/PLAN_BONE_TRACEABILITY.md`, `PLAN_REQUIREMENTS.json` — regenerated via `notes/plan/tools/generate_traceability.py`\n\n**Evidence:** 6 unit tests in `replay.rs` + 6 integration tests, 12 in total — closed accept/refuse discipline checked against all 19 `ArtifactClass` variants (only `Crashpack` accepted, the other 18 each refused by name), exact wire rendering (`Json::String` of the bare handle, no wrapping object), determinism both directions, canonical-JSON round-trip, and a regression pin that `\"replay\"` is not a `SelectionKind` wire token.\n\n**Gates, all exit 0 from workspace root:** `cargo fmt --all --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings`, `cargo test -p continuum-context --locked` (110 tests: 86 unit + 7 IMPL-03 + 6 IMPL-05 + 10 IMPL-06 + 1 compile-fail doctest), full `just check`. Workspace test count: 2,473 (measured baseline before this bone's changes was **2,461**, one above the 2,460 cited in the brief — a pre-existing one-test drift in this workspace snapshot, not something this bone introduced; verified by `git stash`/rerun before applying my changes). Delta: +12, matching the 12 new tests exactly.\n\n**Surprising:** the task's own framing (\"the `replay` selection kind\") doesn't match either normative text — `replay` is a pack-level field, not a `selected[].kind` member, and the module doc/annotation say so with quotes rather than silently building a `SelectionKind::Replay` that would have been a closed-enum breaking change. Also surprising: `crashpack.schema.json` has its own unrelated nested `replay` field (a shell reproduction command), a second, coincidental use of the word one schema layer down from this bullet's actual scope — flagged explicitly in the module doc to head off future confusion.\n\nLeft in `doing`, not merged/closed/pushed."}	blake3:wP4zmTpsfmy9xPxbAG0m8SKAKDLg__K6upKnJKNhKw4
1785873543784452	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy4wo		item.comment	bn-2w2s	{"body":"Lead: reviewed and merged @ epoch a408f3e. The corrective reading is RATIFIED and is the bone's real value: replay is a top-level pack field (crash_* | null), NOT a twelfth selection kind — my brief's framing was wrong and inventing SelectionKind::Replay would have been a closed-enum breaking change without a schema_epoch advance. ReplayRef = one class-checked Crashpack handle on the with_model pattern; the two payload-widening temptations (witness trace = crashpack CONTENT not the handle; crashpack.schema.json's own nested 'replay' = coincidental name collision one layer down) read and declined with quotes. Cross-field C2 rule correctly left to pack assembly; dbg_* correctly left to RFC 0029. Accept-when-given honesty for the unmintable crash_* handle. 110 context tests, 2,473 workspace."}	blake3:85QThtqRHCJkSEvP6ItNNCKBAOb6v7nBCridoWXe3Xo
